    "source": "first assistant implementation notes; unverified; immutable Planner takes precedence",
    "text": "Implementation contract (short):\n\n- Requirement ownership:\n  - All active requirements (indices 0-21) implemented in game/flappy_bird_clone.py (game/__init__.py is empty package marker).\n- State ownership (all in flappy_bird_clone.py):\n  - bird: dict with x(float), y(float), vel_y(float), width(int), height(int), image(surface)\n  - pipes: list of dicts {x(float), gap_y(float), passed(bool)}\n  - score: int\n  - game_over: bool\n  - spawn_timer_ms: int (last spawn tick)\n- Interfaces (functions in flappy_bird_clone.py):\n  - reset_game() -> None : resets bird position/velocity, clears pipes, score=0, game_over=False\n  - spawn_pipe() -> None : appends a pipe dict with x=start_x, gap_y=random, passed=False\n  - check_collisions() -> bool : returns True if collision detected (also sets game_over)\n- Coordinate convention:\n  - Pygame standard: origin (0,0) top-left; y increases downward.\n  - Bird fixed horizontal x (near left); vertical y changes under gravity.\n- Input -> action -> state -> feedback:\n  - KEYDOWN SPACE: set bird.vel_y = JUMP_V (negative), print \"FLAP\", visible bird moves upward next frames.\n  - KEYDOWN R: call reset_game(), print \"RESTART\".\n  - KEYDOWN Escape or QUIT event: print \"QUIT\" and exit.\n  - Collisions or bird out of bounds: set game_over True, print \"GAME OVER\", stop updating positions, draw \"GAME OVER\" and final score.\n- Lifecycle:\n  - init: load assets, set window title \"Flappy Bird Clone\", set initial game state via reset_game().\n  - run: main loop updates physics (if not game_over), spawn pipes at interval, scroll pipes, handle input, draw background, bird, pipes, score.\n  - terminal: on game_over freeze motions until R pressed to reset.\n  - reset: reset_game restores starting positions, clears pipes and score.\n  - quit: Escape key or window close event exits process.\n\nNow I'll write the promised files.",
    "truncated": false
  },
